cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CorpusPrep: corpus preparation for linguists"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adesokan
    given-names: Tosin
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-08-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adesokantosin2000-beep/corpusprep"
abstract: >-
  CorpusPrep prepares source texts for corpus analysis. Every line of a
  document is labelled before anything is removed, so the researcher decides
  what constitutes the corpus, and an accompanying log records how that
  decision was made. Handles Project Gutenberg apparatus, front and back
  matter, chapter and act segmentation, and TXT, DOCX, EPUB and HTML import.
keywords:
  - corpus linguistics
  - text preprocessing
  - digital humanities
  - reproducibility
